# Configuration

The application loads its configuration from environment variables.

A local `.env` file is expected at the project root.

Typical configuration values include:

```env
DB_DSN=...
SECRET_KEY=...
REDIS_ADDR=...
REDIS_PASSWORD=...
REDIS_DB=...
```

Sensitive values such as database credentials and JWT secrets should remain outside version control.

---

# Running the Project

Make sure PostgreSQL and Redis are running and the required environment variables are configured.

From the project root:

```bash
go run ./cmd
```

The HTTP API starts on:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

Swagger documentation:

```text
http://localhost:8080/swagger/index.html
```

A separate profiling endpoint is also initialized on port `6060`.

